=========================================================
PROJECT OVERVIEW
=========================================================
The Asset Management System is a console-based application
developed using the C Programming Language.
The system is designed to assist organizations in managing
their assets by providing facilities to add, search,
update, delete, display, save and load asset records.
The system stores information about organizational assets
including their identification number, name, type,
department, condition and purchase value. 【1-c73106】
=========================================================
FUNCTIONALITIES IMPLEMENTED
=========================================================
1. Add Asset
Captures new asset details into the system.
---------------------------------------------------------
2. Display Assets
Displays all asset records stored in the system.
---------------------------------------------------------
3. Search Asset
Allows searching for assets using:
- Asset ID
- Asset Name
---------------------------------------------------------
4. Update Asset
Allows modification of existing asset details.
---------------------------------------------------------
5. Delete Asset
Removes an existing asset record from the system.
---------------------------------------------------------
6. Sort Assets
Sorts asset records alphabetically.
---------------------------------------------------------
7. Save Assets
Saves asset records into a file.
---------------------------------------------------------
8. Load Assets
Loads asset records from a file.
=========================================================
ASSET INFORMATION STORED
=========================================================
The system stores:
- Asset ID
- Asset Name
- Asset Type
- Asset Department
- Asset Condition
- Purchase Value
【1-c73106】
=========================================================
ASSET TYPES AVAILABLE
=========================================================
The system allows selection of various asset types such as:
- Vehicle
- Computer
- Equipment
- Building
- Furniture
- Infrastructure